    {
      "id": "d2ed7145-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement is subject to revision without prior notice. Please check with a counselor every semester to obtain current information about possible changes in the agreement. To learn more about the courses and programs offered at Sonoma State University or the General Education and Upper-division requirements for each major please refer to the university catalog at: http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/",
      "contentHtml": "This agreement is subject to revision without prior notice.  Please check with a counselor every semester to obtain current information about possible changes in the agreement.  To learn more about the courses and programs offered at Sonoma State University or the General Education and Upper-division requirements for each major please refer to the university catalog at: <a href=\"http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/</a>"
    },
    {
      "id": "8a007045-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MATHEMATICS AND STATISTICS MAJORS AND MINORS: A mathematics and statistics major or minor must take all mathematics and statistics courses in the traditional grading mode, with the exceptions of courses offered only in CR/NC modes and any course taken as credit by challenge examination.",
      "contentHtml": "MATHEMATICS AND STATISTICS MAJORS AND MINORS: A mathematics and statistics major or minor must take all mathematics and statistics courses in the traditional grading mode, with the exceptions of courses offered only in CR/NC modes and any course taken as credit by challenge examination."
    },
    {
      "id": "fc007045-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "The AS-T in Mathematics (SB 1440 degree) has been deemed a &quot;similar&quot; degree to the Mathematics, B.S.: Applied Mathematics Concentration at Sonoma State. Students transfering to SSU with an AS-T in Mathematics are advised to complete all available articulated major requirement and support courses before transfer. It is also recommended that students complete the American Instutitions (US-1, US-2, US-3), and Seawolf Studies Graduation requirements before transfer.",
      "contentHtml": "The AS-T in Mathematics (SB 1440 degree) has been deemed a &quot;similar&quot; degree to the Mathematics, B.S.: Applied Mathematics Concentration at Sonoma State.  Students transfering to SSU with an AS-T in Mathematics are advised to complete all available articulated major requirement and support courses before transfer.  It is also recommended that students complete the American Instutitions (US-1, US-2, US-3), and Seawolf Studies Graduation requirements before transfer."
    }
